<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/RelationshipType/delegatedTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The `from` Agent is delegating an action to the Agent of the `to` Relationship (which shall be of type invokedBy), during a LifecycleScopeType (e.g. the `to` invokedBy Relationship is being done on behalf of `from`)."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/CreationInfo> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#property> _:N470c2e9c9e7d4749a9d3dc720ad37ad0 .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/RelationshipType/follows> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The `to` Element succeeds the `from` Element, establishing a unidirectional sequence. This succession is defined as chronological, procedural, or logical. It is used to represent either a temporal order (e.g., in a workflow) or a logical order for processing and traversal (e.g., in an ordered list)."@en .
